  "tagline": "The Btrieve/Pervasive lineage: zero-admin embedded database with key-level and SQL access, now edge-focused.",
  "description": "Actian Zen is the current name for the database that began as Btrieve in 1982 and later became Pervasive PSQL. Its trick is dual access to the same files: a fast record-level Btrieve 2 API for navigational reads and writes, and a relational SQL engine with ODBC/JDBC on top. That made it a favourite for accounting, practice-management and retail ISVs that ship a database inside their product and need it to run unattended. Actian, now part of HCLSoftware, released Zen 16.0 in June 2024 with larger key sizes, Kafka streaming, EasySync replication and container support. It is best for existing Btrieve applications and small embedded/edge deployments.",
